  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Modernisierung von medizinischen Multiprofil-Zentren der Gebietsebene in vier Regionen der Republik Usbekistan</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Modernization of 4 medical multi disciplinary regional Centres</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das Programmziel besteht in der Verbesserung der Qualit&#xe4;t, Effizienz und Nachhaltigkeit der medizinischen Versorgung in den Multiprofil-Zentren der Gebietsebene in den Programmregionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the program is to improve the quality, efficiency and sustainability of medical care in the multidisciplinary medical centers of Nukus (Republic of Karakalpakstan), Navoi (Navoiyskaya oblast), Andijan (Andijanskaya oblast) and Bukhara (Bukharskaya oblast). This is to be achieved by modernizing medical equipment, introducing modern care methods and implementing rationalization and optimization measures. This is intended to contribute to the overarching development policy objective of improving the health of the population as a whole. The target group of the project is primarily the rural population of Uzbekistan. The total population of the regions is around 7.2 million people. The total costs of the program are estimated at EUR 20.9 million, of which EUR 10.0 million (EUR 9.0 million - investment and EUR 1.0 million - complementary measure) are to be financed by FC funds and approx. EUR 10.9 million by Uzbekistans own contribution.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das Programmziel ist es, Qualit&#xe4;t, Effizienz und Nachhaltigkeit der medizinischen Versorgung in den multidisziplin&#xe4;ren medizinischen Zentren von Nukus (Republik Karakalpakstan), Navoij (Navoijskaja Oblast), Andijan (Andijanskaja Oblast) sowie Buchara (Bucharskaja Oblast) zu verbessern. Dies soll durch Modernisierung der medizinischen Ausstattung, Einf&#xfc;hrung von modernen Versorgungsmethoden, Umsetzung von Rationalisierungs- und Optimierungsma&#xdf;nahmen erreicht werden. Dadurch soll ein Beitrag zum &#xfc;bergeordneten entwicklungspolitischen Ziel, der Verbesserung des Gesundheitszustandes der Gesamtbev&#xf6;lkerung, geleistet werden. Die Zielgruppe des Vorhabens ist im Wesentlichen die l&#xe4;ndliche Bev&#xf6;lkerung Usbekistans. Die Einwohnerzahl der Regionen betr&#xe4;gt in Summe rd. 7,2 Mio. Menschen. Die Gesamtkosten des Programms werden auf 20,9 Mio. EUR gesch&#xe4;tzt, davon sollen 10,0 Mio. EUR (9,0 Mio. EUR - Investition und 1,0 Mio. EUR - Begleitma&#xdf;nahme) durch FZ-Mittel und ca. 10,9 Mio. EUR durch usbekische Eigenleistung finanziert werden.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the program is to improve the quality, efficiency and sustainability of medical care in the multidisciplinary medical centers of Nukus (Republic of Karakalpakstan), Navoi (Navoiyskaya oblast), Andijan (Andijanskaya oblast) and Bukhara (Bukharskaya oblast). This is to be achieved by modernizing medical equipment, introducing modern care methods and implementing rationalization and optimization measures. This is intended to contribute to the overarching development policy objective of improving the health of the population as a whole. The target group of the project is primarily the rural population of Uzbekistan. The total population of the regions is around 7.2 million people. The total costs of the program are estimated at EUR 20.9 million, of which EUR 10.0 million (EUR 9.0 million - investment and EUR 1.0 million - complementary measure) are to be financed by FC funds and approx. EUR 10.9 million by Uzbekistans own contribution.</narrative>
  </description>
